Relevant columns and possible usage  
• "publication_number": identifies each patent publication that will appear in the final answer.  
• "grant_date": lets us keep only patents granted in the 2010‑2018 window (assumes YYYYMMDD numeric format).  
• "citation": VARIANT that contains the backward‑citation list; needs to be flattened to inspect each cited document.  
• "citation"."category" (inside VARIANT): expected place where the citation type such as “SEA” is stored; used to isolate “SEA” citations only.  

Typical filter conditions  
• "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231  
• "citation" IS NOT NULL  
• f.value:"category"::STRING ILIKE 'SEA%'   -- after FLATTEN

Ten exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets  
```sql
--1------------------------------------------------------------
--Description: Quick look at patents granted 2010‑2018.
SELECT "publication_number",
       "grant_date"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE  "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;

--2------------------------------------------------------------
--Description: Same patents but be sure they have citation data.
SELECT "publication_number",
       "grant_date",
       "citation"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE  "grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
  AND  "citation" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;

--3------------------------------------------------------------
--Description: Inspect raw JSON elements inside one patent’s citation array.
SELECT f.value AS "raw_citation_json"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") f
WHERE  t."publication_number" = 'US-7650331-B1'        --replace with any sample
LIMIT 20;

--4------------------------------------------------------------
--Description: Peek at common keys of the citation object to locate the “category” field.
SELECT DISTINCT
       OBJECT_KEYS(f.value) AS "citation_keys"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") f
WHERE  t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;

--5------------------------------------------------------------
--Description: Show each backward citation with its category text if present.
SELECT t."publication_number",
       f.value:"publication_number"::STRING  AS "cited_pub_no",
       f.value:"category"::STRING            AS "cite_category"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") f
WHERE  t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;

--6------------------------------------------------------------
--Description: Count all citations per patent, regardless of category.
SELECT t."publication_number",
       COUNT(*) AS "total_citations"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") f
WHERE  t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
GROUP BY t."publication_number"
ORDER BY "total_citations" DESC
LIMIT 20;

--7------------------------------------------------------------
--Description: Count “SEA” citations specifically (case‑insensitive match).
SELECT t."publication_number",
       COUNT(*) AS "sea_citations"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") f
WHERE  t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
  AND  f.value:"category"::STRING ILIKE 'SEA%'
GROUP BY t."publication_number"
ORDER BY "sea_citations" DESC
LIMIT 20;

--8------------------------------------------------------------
--Description: Return only patents that have at least one SEA citation.
SELECT DISTINCT t."publication_number"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") f
WHERE  t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
  AND  f.value:"category"::STRING ILIKE 'SEA%'
LIMIT 20;

--9------------------------------------------------------------
--Description: Combine grant year extraction with SEA citation count.
SELECT TO_CHAR(t."grant_date", 'YYYY') AS "grant_year",
       COUNT(*)                        AS "num_pats_with_sea"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t
WHERE  t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
  AND  EXISTS ( SELECT 1
                FROM   LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") f
                WHERE  f.value:"category"::STRING ILIKE 'SEA%' )
GROUP BY TO_CHAR(t."grant_date", 'YYYY')
ORDER BY "grant_year"
LIMIT 20;

--10-----------------------------------------------------------
--Description: Final‑style query – publication number and SEA backward‑citation count.
SELECT t."publication_number",
       COUNT(*) AS "sea_citation_count"
FROM   PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") f
WHERE  t."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231
  AND  f.value:"category"::STRING ILIKE 'SEA%'
GROUP BY t."publication_number"
ORDER BY t."publication_number"
LIMIT 20;
```
